# Cursor Rules for Eventia Project

# IMPORTANT (ALWAYS):
# Always read memory-bank/architecture.md before writing any code. Include entire database schema.
# Always read memory-bank/product-requirements-document.md before writing any code.
# Always read memory-bank/project-best-practices.md before writing any code.
# After adding a major feature or completing a milestone, update memory-bank/architecture.md.
# After completing an implementation step, update memory-bank/progress.md.

# REACT DEVELOPMENT RULES:
Use React with TypeScript for all frontend development.
Implement React components as function components with hooks.
Use React Query for server state management.
Organize components by feature in the components directory.
Implement proper error handling in all API calls.
Use Tailwind CSS for styling.
Ensure mobile-first responsive design.

# MONGODB DEVELOPMENT RULES:
Use Mongoose for MongoDB schema definition and validation.
Implement proper indexing for frequently queried fields.
Use MongoDB aggregation pipeline for complex queries.
Implement optimistic concurrency control for critical operations.
Always validate data before saving to database.

# CODE QUALITY RULES:
Follow the TypeScript best practices.
Keep functions small and focused on a single responsibility.
Write meaningful comments for complex logic.
Implement comprehensive error handling.
Use async/await for asynchronous operations.
Follow a consistent naming convention.

# AUTHENTICATION RULES:
Use JWT for authentication with refresh tokens.
Implement proper password hashing with bcrypt.
Add rate limiting for authentication endpoints.
Validate all user inputs with Zod.
Implement role-based access control.

# UI/UX RULES:
Implement loading states for all async operations.
Provide meaningful error messages to users.
Create a consistent UI across the application.
Ensure proper form validation with helpful messages.
Implement accessibility features (ARIA labels, keyboard navigation).

# PAYMENT PROCESSING RULES:
Implement secure UPI payment flow.
Add proper logging for all payment operations.
Implement robust UTR verification workflow.
Handle payment timeouts and failures gracefully.

# TESTING RULES:
Write unit tests for all business logic.
Implement integration tests for API endpoints.
Add end-to-end tests for critical user flows.
Test responsive design across different screen sizes.

# RISK MANAGEMENT RULES:
Identify potential risks before implementing each feature.
Document security considerations for sensitive operations.
Create contingency plans for high-traffic periods during IPL season.
Implement proper error boundary handling in React components. 

